P0 MONEY / DURABILITY / AUTHORITY REVIEW

1. =E2=80=9Cdurable store=E2=80=9D is currently not durable.
Current tree has src/store/types.ts + src/store/memory.ts only.
MemoryStore disappears on restart and mutations are non-atomic.
Do not call this durable.

Implement ONE actual transactional store now.
Recommended first target:
- SQLite WAL for single-instance MVP
- Postgres implementation immediately after if multi-instance is needed.

Required DB invariants:
- sessions.id PK
- invoices.id PK
- UNIQUE(invoice subaddress major/minor or unique address commitment
as appropriate)
- UNIQUE(invoice_id, capability_type) so callback cannot double-mint
- capabilities.token_hash UNIQUE
- grants.nonce UNIQUE per issuer
- effects.idempotency_key UNIQUE per scope
- receipt/log metadata immutable
- state transition rows append-only

Use actual transactions:
payment settlement + credit ledger + capability mint MUST be one transactio=
n.
grant consume + effect PREPARE MUST be one transaction/reservation.
Use BEGIN IMMEDIATE/CAS on SQLite or SELECT ... FOR UPDATE /
serializable transaction on Postgres.

Tests must include:
- 50 concurrent duplicate payment callbacks -> one capability
- 50 concurrent grant uses with max_uses=3D1 -> one succeeds
- crash after provider request before readback -> restart ->
reconcile, no duplicate spend
- restart after every state in journal
- database corruption/error =3D> effect fails closed, never =E2=80=9Cbest e=
ffort=E2=80=9D.

2. Current XMR implementation is calling wallet-rpc incorrectly.

Official wallet RPC:
https://docs.getmonero.org/rpc-library/wallet-rpc/

For a fresh subaddress use:
method=3Dcreate_address
params=3D{account_index, label, count}
returns address + address_index.

Current pmail createSubAddress uses make_integrated_address and
expects subaddress_index. That is wrong.

For incoming transfer observation:
method=3Dget_transfers
params=3D{
  in:true,
  account_index:<major>,
  subaddr_indices:[<minor>],
  pool:true/false according policy
}
incoming confirmed transfers are in result.in, not result.transfers.

Current pmail sends {filter:"received", subaddr_indices:[...]} and
reads response.transfers. Fix it.

A transfer observation must evaluate:
- exact account/subaddress major+minor
- exact expected invoice
- aggregate ALL relevant incoming amounts, including partial payments
- confirmations >=3D policy threshold
- double_spend_seen =3D=3D=3D false
- sane/unlocked state
- transaction identity deduplication
- wallet/daemon synced enough to make observation meaningful
- pool/0-conf explicitly distinct from confirmed
- RPC outage/parser error =3D> UNKNOWN, never FALSE

3. Prefer actual MoneroPay sidecar instead of rebuilding payment lifecycle.

Repo:
https://github.com/moneropay/moneropay
GPL-3.0, keep as separate process/service.

It already supports:
- subaddress-based incoming payments
- partial payments
- HTTP callbacks
- timelock handling
- SQLite/Postgres
- view-only/hot wallets
- unlock callbacks
- optional 0-conf

PMail integration:
A. MoneroPay =3D payment orchestration/event source
B. wallet-rpc =3D independent canonical wallet observer before minting
high-value capability
C. QP =3D exact semantic settlement
D. DB transaction =3D capability/credit issuance

Default policy: DO NOT mint final capability from 0-conf.
If a low-risk service intentionally allows 0-conf, represent separate
actuality/assurance level in ProofSpec.

4. Invoice privacy.
Do not publish sha256(address) as a naked deterministic commitment.
Use:
commitment =3D SHA256("pmail-invoice-v1" || random_32_byte_nonce ||
address || invoice_id)
Keep nonce/address private.
Public receipt gets commitment only.

5. LocalAuthority is not production authority.

Current src/authority/grantex.ts LocalAuthority:
- generates its own Ed25519 key in process
- issueGrant accepts arbitrary caller-provided issuer string
- verify checks LocalAuthority key but does not require claimed issuer
=3D=3D configured issuer
=3D> issuer-confusion: token may claim =E2=80=9Chuman:owner=E2=80=9D while =
signed by
local service key.

Also:
- maxAmount/currency arguments are not independently enforced against effec=
t
- constraint object is signed but validateGrant does not evaluate
proposed provider/resource/price/scopes
- ttlSeconds || 3600 and maxUses || 1 replace explicit zero
- consume is separate from validate =3D> TOCTOU
- in-memory activeGrants vanish on restart.

FIX:
Production grant issuer must be an external trusted principal/operator iden=
tity.
QP effect authorization requires:
  trusted issuer
  subject/agent
  action
  exact canonical proposal/payload hash
  constraints_root
  provider/resource
  max amount + currency
  scopes
  issued_at + bounded future skew
  expires_at
  nonce
  max uses
  revocation status
  idempotency binding

Then consume atomically with PREPARE.

Upstream option:
https://github.com/mishrasanjeev/grantex
Current researched TS SDK release: @grantex/sdk 0.6.0.
Protocol includes scoped/time-limited/revocable grants, JWKS
verification and delegation.
For ANON_CORE:
- self-host or use its protocol/SDK with pseudonymous principal IDs
- do not introduce hosted email/identity requirement just to gain auth
- QP exact proposal/price constraints remain our layer even if Grantex
scope token is valid.

Delete the current class name =E2=80=9CLocalAuthority=E2=80=9D from product=
ion
bootstrap. Keep as DEV_ONLY test signer only.

6. Effect journal.
Current journal semantics must be persisted:
PROPOSED
-> AUTHORIZED
-> PREPARED
-> EXECUTING
-> EXECUTED_UNVERIFIED
-> PROVEN_TRUE | PROVEN_FALSE | UNKNOWN_RECONCILE

Every transition:
- validates allowed prior state
- compare-and-swap version
- persists attempt number
- provider request id/idempotency key
- immutable effect spec root
- exact proposal root
- authority root
- response commitment if one happened
- resulting claim id
- timestamps

Never silently ignore invalid/missing transition.

Acceptance demo:
stagenet or isolated controlled wallet:
1. create session
2. real new subaddress
3. pay in parts
4. first partial =3D> not funded
5. remaining payment =3D> observe exact total
6. wait required confirmations
7. one DB transaction settles payment, credits session, mints capability
8. replay callback 100x =3D> no extra credit
9. restart process =3D> state persists
10. QP payment receipt semantically replays
11. public receipt reveals no address/tx id.
